# Security headers for the Expo web build (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING: this file does NOT cover the HTML document.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pages applies `_headers` to STATIC ASSET responses only. This project runs in
# advanced mode (`dist/_worker.js`, copied from `public/_worker.js` by the export),
# so every HTML
# navigation is answered by a Response that Worker constructs — and Cloudflare
# does not apply `_headers` to responses generated by a Function. The document
# policy therefore lives in `public/_worker.js` (`CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY` +
# `withSecurityHeaders`), which is what actually reaches a browser.
#
# This file remains the policy for the assets Pages serves directly, and is the
# fallback if advanced mode is ever dropped. The CSP below must stay byte-identical
# to the worker's — `scripts/verify-web-build.mjs` fails the build on drift, so a
# change here without a matching change there will not deploy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSP notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  - Metro's web bundle and Razorpay's checkout both need 'unsafe-inline' for
#    styles; scripts are restricted to self plus the Razorpay checkout SDK.
#  - frame-src allows the Razorpay checkout iframe and Firebase auth handlers.
#  - Framing THIS app is allowed from nowhere, which also protects the
#    login/payment screens from being embedded.
#  - connect-src needs blob: because on web the image/video picker hands us a
#    blob: URI and uploadToR2() does fetch(uri) to read it back into a Blob.
#    fetch() is governed by connect-src, so without blob: every contest entry,
#    story, avatar and deposit-slip upload died with "Failed to fetch".
#    img-src/media-src already allowed blob:, which is why previews rendered
#    fine and made this look like a network bug instead of a CSP one.
#  - connect-src lists wss://api.tophunt.in as well as https://. Realtime push
#    (src/services/realtime.ts) derives its socket URL from the API base by
#    swapping the scheme, and CSP matches scheme-by-scheme — an https:// entry
#    does not authorise the wss:// connection. Omitting it kills live votes, chat
#    delivery and the notification badge while every plain fetch keeps working.
#  - The media hosts are listed because media is FETCHED, not only displayed:
#    battle-card share/download and the web VS capture call fetch() on an image
#    URL, and that is connect-src, not img-src.
#  - The legacy `tophunt-api.weadown-in.workers.dev` host stays until the media
#    backfill has run: pre-cutover rows still hold absolute URLs on it.
#  - static.cloudflareinsights.com / cloudflareinsights.com are Cloudflare Web
#    Analytics. Pages injects that beacon into every HTML response when the
#    feature is enabled for the project, so omitting it means a CSP violation
#    on every page load — the app cannot opt out from its own side.
#  - Hosts are pinned exactly rather than via https://*.workers.dev. That
#    wildcard authorised every Cloudflare customer's Worker as a destination for
#    a page that handles logins and wallet balances. The staging Worker is named
#    explicitly instead, so preview deployments still work.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://checkout.razorpay.com https://*.gstatic.com https://*.googleapis.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://api.tophunt.in wss://api.tophunt.in https://media.tophunt.in https://video.bunnycdn.com https://*.b-cdn.net https://tophunt-api.weadown-in.workers.dev wss://tophunt-api.weadown-in.workers.dev https://tophunt-api-staging.weadown-in.workers.dev wss://tophunt-api-staging.weadown-in.workers.dev https://*.googleapis.com https://*.firebaseio.com wss://*.firebaseio.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://lumberjack.razorpay.com https://api.razorpay.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://api.razorpay.com https://checkout.razorpay.com https://*.firebaseapp.com; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# The service worker must not be cached, or push registration can go stale.
/firebase-messaging-sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /
